    'colonelganj' => 'Colonelganj is a town in Gonda district of eastern Uttar Pradesh, on the banks of the Saryu. It is easily combined with trips to Gonda and Ayodhya.',
    'dabra' => 'Dabra is a town in Gwalior district of Madhya Pradesh on the Gwalior–Jhansi highway. Gwalior Fort and the Datia palace and Pitambara Peeth are a short drive away.',
    'dakpatthar' => 'Dakpatthar is a small town in Dehradun district of Uttarakhand on the Yamuna, known for its barrage and reservoir. The Ashokan rock edict at Kalsi is close by.',
    'dalhousie' => 'Dalhousie is a colonial-era hill station in Chamba district of Himachal Pradesh, spread over five hills. It is known for old churches, pine forests, Panchpula and its closeness to Khajjiar, the "Mini Switzerland of India".',
    'damoh' => 'Damoh is a district town in Madhya Pradesh\'s Bundelkhand region. The Kundalpur Jain pilgrimage centre and the Nohleshwar temple are nearby.',
    'dasuya' => 'Dasuya is a town in Hoshiarpur district of Punjab on the Jalandhar–Pathankot highway. It lies on the way to Mukerian, Pathankot and the hills of Himachal.',
    'daulatpur' => 'Daulatpur is a town in Una district of Himachal Pradesh. It is close to the Chintpurni temple and easy to combine with a temple tour of the region.',
    'dausa' => 'Dausa is a district town in Rajasthan on the Jaipur–Agra highway. It is close to the Mehandipur Balaji Temple and the Chand Baori stepwell at Abhaneri.',
    'deeg' => 'Deeg in Rajasthan\'s Bharatpur district is known for its beautiful palace gardens and the Jal Mahal, whose hundreds of fountains still run on special occasions. It is an easy add-on to trips to Mathura and Bharatpur.',
    'deoband' => 'Deoband is a town in Saharanpur district of Uttar Pradesh, home to the Darul Uloom Deoband, one of the most influential Islamic seminaries in the world. The Devi Kund temple is a local landmark.',
    'derabassi' => 'Dera Bassi is a town in Mohali district of Punjab on the Ambala–Chandigarh highway. It is next to Zirakpur and a short drive from Chandigarh.',
    'devala' => 'Devala is a small place in Uttarakhand\'s hill region. Share your exact location and we will plan the best route and pickup timing for your group.',
    'devprayag' => 'Devprayag in Tehri Garhwal is where the Alaknanda and Bhagirathi rivers meet to form the Ganga. The confluence and the ancient Raghunath Temple make it a holy stop on the Char Dham route.',
    'dhamnod' => 'Dhamnod is a town in Dhar district of Madhya Pradesh on the Agra–Mumbai highway. It is close to Mandu and the Narmada ghats of Maheshwar.',
    'dhampur' => 'Dhampur is a town in Bijnor district of western Uttar Pradesh, known for its sugar mills. It is easily combined with trips to Bijnor and Kashipur.',
    'dhanaulti' => 'Dhanaulti is a quiet hill station in Tehri Garhwal, Uttarakhand, about 25 km beyond Mussoorie. It is known for its Eco Park, deodar forests, apple orchards and the Surkanda Devi Temple.',
    'dhanaura' => 'Dhanaura is a town in Amroha district of western Uttar Pradesh. It is easily combined with trips to Amroha and Moradabad.',
    'dhanera' => 'Dhanera is a town in Banaskantha district of north Gujarat near the Rajasthan border. It is easily combined with trips to Palanpur and Mount Abu.',
    'dharampur' => 'Dharampur is a small town in Solan district of Himachal Pradesh on the Kalka–Shimla highway. Kasauli and the Sanawar school are a short drive away.',
    'dharchula' => 'Dharchula is a border town in Pithoragarh district of Uttarakhand on the Kali river, facing Nepal. It is a base for the Adi Kailash and Om Parvat routes and for Narayan Ashram.',
    'dhariwal' => 'Dhariwal is a town in Gurdaspur district of Punjab, known for its historic woollen mill. It is easily combined with trips to Gurdaspur, Batala and Amritsar.',
    'dharuhera' => 'Dharuhera is an industrial town in Rewari district of Haryana on the Delhi–Jaipur highway. It is a frequent business and staff-transport route from Delhi and Gurugram.',
    'dholpur' => 'Dholpur in Rajasthan sits on the Chambal river, known for its red sandstone used in many landmark buildings. The Machkund sacred lake, Shergarh Fort and the Van Vihar sanctuary are the main sights.',
    'dhuri' => 'Dhuri is a town in Sangrur district of Punjab and an important railway junction. It is easily combined with trips to Sangrur and Malerkotla.',
    'dibai' => 'Dibai is a town in Bulandshahr district of western Uttar Pradesh near the Ganga. It is close to the ghats of Narora and Anupshahar.',
    'didwana' => 'Didwana is a town in Nagaur district of Rajasthan, known for its salt lake. The Pada Mata Temple is a local landmark, and Ladnun\'s Jain centre is nearby.',
    'doiwala' => 'Doiwala is a town in Dehradun district of Uttarakhand, right next to Jolly Grant Airport. It is a common pickup point for trips to Rishikesh, Dehradun and Mussoorie.',
    'doraha' => 'Doraha is a town in Ludhiana district of Punjab on the GT Road. It is known for its highway dhabas and lies a short drive from Ludhiana.',
    'dugadda' => 'Dugadda is a small town in Pauri Garhwal, Uttarakhand, on the road from Kotdwar to Lansdowne. It is a gateway to Lansdowne and the Garhwal hills.',
    'dungarpur' => 'Dungarpur in southern Rajasthan is known for its unique architecture in grey-blue local stone. Juna Mahal, Udai Bilas Palace and Gaib Sagar Lake are the highlights.',
    'dwarahat' => 'Dwarahat in Almora district of Uttarakhand is known for its group of ancient Katyuri-era temples. The Dunagiri Devi temple and Pandukholi are nearby.',
    'etah' => 'Etah is a district town in western Uttar Pradesh between Aligarh and Mainpuri. It is easily combined with trips to Kasganj and Soron.',
    'etawah' => 'Etawah is a city in Uttar Pradesh on the Yamuna, best known for the Etawah Lion Safari. The National Chambal Sanctuary and Sumer Singh Fort are nearby.',
    'fagu' => 'Fagu is a small hill village near Kufri in Shimla district of Himachal Pradesh. It is known for apple orchards, misty valleys and views of the snow peaks.',
    'faizabad' => 'Faizabad is the twin city of Ayodhya in Uttar Pradesh, once the capital of the Nawabs of Awadh. Gulab Bari, the Bahu Begum ka Maqbara and the Saryu ghats are its landmarks.',
    'falna' => 'Falna is a town in Pali district of Rajasthan and a busy railway station. It is the nearest railhead for the Ranakpur Jain Temple and the Jawai leopard area.',
    'faridabad' => 'Faridabad is Haryana\'s largest city, just south of Delhi. Surajkund, famous for its crafts fair, Badkhal Lake and the Raja Nahar Singh Palace are local attractions.',
    'faridkot' => 'Faridkot is a historic city in Punjab, once a princely state. The Qila Mubarak fort and Tilla Baba Farid, linked to the Sufi saint Baba Farid, are its best-known sights.',
    'farrukhabad' => 'Farrukhabad is a city on the Ganga in Uttar Pradesh. It is known for textile printing, and the Buddhist site of Sankisa is nearby.',
    'fatehabad' => 'Fatehabad is a district town in Haryana between Hisar and Sirsa. The Harappan site of Banawali is close by.',
    'fatehpur' => 'Fatehpur is a district town in Uttar Pradesh between Kanpur and Prayagraj. The Bhitargaon brick temple, one of the oldest in India, is nearby.',
    'fatehpur-sikri' => 'Fatehpur Sikri, near Agra, was Emperor Akbar\'s capital and is now a UNESCO World Heritage Site. The Buland Darwaza, Jama Masjid, Salim Chishti\'s Dargah and Panch Mahal are its highlights.',
    'fazilka' => 'Fazilka is a border town in Punjab, close to Pakistan. The Sadqi border retreat ceremony and the town\'s old Ghanta Ghar are its main attractions.',
    'ferozepur' => 'Ferozepur is a historic border city in Punjab. The Hussainiwala border, the National Martyrs Memorial of Bhagat Singh, Rajguru and Sukhdev, and the Saragarhi Memorial are the main sights.',
    'firozabad' => 'Firozabad in Uttar Pradesh is India\'s glass and bangle city, producing most of the country\'s glass bangles. It is a short drive from Agra.',
    'gadarpur' => 'Gadarpur is a town in Udham Singh Nagar district of Uttarakhand. It is easily combined with trips to Rudrapur, Kashipur and the Kumaon hills.',
    'gajraula' => 'Gajraula is an industrial town in Amroha district of Uttar Pradesh on NH-9. It lies on the way from Delhi to Moradabad and the Kumaon hills.',
    'ganaur' => 'Ganaur is a town in Sonipat district of Haryana on the GT Road (NH-44). It is easily combined with trips to Sonipat and Panipat.',
    'gangapur-city' => 'Gangapur City is a town in Sawai Madhopur district of Rajasthan. It is close to the Mehandipur Balaji and Kaila Devi temples.',
    'gangoh' => 'Gangoh is a town in Saharanpur district of western Uttar Pradesh, known for its Sufi shrines. It is easily combined with trips to Saharanpur.',
    'gangotri' => 'Gangotri is one of the four Char Dham shrines, set at about 3,100 m in Uttarkashi district. The Gangotri Temple stands near the source of the Ganga, and it is the starting point of the trek to Gaumukh glacier.',
    'ganj-dundwara' => 'Ganj Dundwara is a town in Kasganj district of Uttar Pradesh. It is easily combined with trips to Kasganj and Soron.',
    'garh-mukteshwar' => 'Garh Mukteshwar is a holy town on the Ganga in Hapur district, the closest Ganga ghat to Delhi. Brajghat, the Mukteshwar Mahadev Temple and the Kartik Purnima fair draw large crowds.',
    'gaurikund' => 'Gaurikund in Rudraprayag district is the road head for the Kedarnath trek. It has a hot spring and the Gauri Devi temple, and is the last stop before the 16 km walk to Kedarnath.',
    'gharaunda' => 'Gharaunda is a town in Karnal district of Haryana on the GT Road. It is easily combined with trips to Karnal and Panipat.',
    'ghatampur' => 'Ghatampur is a town in Kanpur Nagar district of Uttar Pradesh. It is easily combined with trips to Kanpur.',
    'ghaziabad' => 'Ghaziabad is a large city in Uttar Pradesh on Delhi\'s eastern border and part of the NCR. It is a frequent pickup and drop point, with the ISKCON temple, the Dudheshwar Nath Temple and City Forest among its sights.',
    'ghoti-budruk' => 'Ghoti is a town in Nashik district of Maharashtra on the Mumbai–Nashik highway, close to Igatpuri. Bhandardara and Trimbakeshwar are nearby. It is a long-distance trip from Delhi.',
    'ghumarwin' => 'Ghumarwin is a town in Bilaspur district of Himachal Pradesh. It is easily combined with trips to Bilaspur, Hamirpur and the Gobind Sagar lake.',
    'gogunda' => 'Gogunda is a historic town near Udaipur in Rajasthan, where Maharana Pratap was crowned. It lies on the route between Udaipur and Kumbhalgarh.',
    'gohana' => 'Gohana is a town in Sonipat district of Haryana, known for its famous jalebis. It is easily combined with trips to Rohtak and Sonipat.',
    'gonda' => 'Gonda is a district town in eastern Uttar Pradesh near Ayodhya. The Prithvinath Temple and the Parvati Arga bird sanctuary are nearby.',
    'gorakhpur' => 'Gorakhpur is a major city in eastern Uttar Pradesh, home to the Gorakhnath Temple and Gita Press. Ramgarh Tal is a popular lakefront, and Kushinagar, where the Buddha attained Mahaparinirvana, is about 50 km away.',
    'govardhan' => 'Govardhan in Mathura district is one of the holiest places in Braj, where Lord Krishna lifted Govardhan Hill. The 21 km Govardhan Parikrama, Radha Kund and Mansi Ganga draw devotees all year.',
    'greater-noida' => 'Greater Noida is a planned city in Uttar Pradesh just south-east of Delhi. It is home to the India Expo Mart, the Buddh International Circuit and the Surajpur bird sanctuary, and is a common pickup point for Agra trips.',
    'guna' => 'Guna is a district town in Madhya Pradesh on the Agra–Mumbai highway. The Bajrang Garh Fort is nearby, and the historic weaving town of Chanderi is a short drive away.',
    'gurdaspur' => 'Gurdaspur is a district town in northern Punjab near the Pakistan border. The historic town of Kalanaur, where Akbar was crowned, and the gurdwaras of Batala are nearby.',
    'gurgaon' => 'Gurugram (Gurgaon) is the corporate hub of Delhi NCR in Haryana. It is a frequent pickup point for outstation trips, with Cyber Hub, Kingdom of Dreams, Sultanpur Bird Sanctuary and Damdama Lake as local attractions.',
    'gwalior' => 'Gwalior in Madhya Pradesh is crowned by the mighty Gwalior Fort, with the Saas-Bahu temples and Man Mandir palace inside. The Jai Vilas Palace and the tomb of the musician Tansen make it a rich heritage trip.',
    'haldaur' => 'Haldaur is a town in Bijnor district of western Uttar Pradesh. It is easily combined with trips to Bijnor.',
    'haldwani' => 'Haldwani is the largest city in the Kumaon region of Uttarakhand and the gateway to Nainital, Bhimtal and Almora. Kathgodam railway station is right next to it.',
    'hamirpur' => 'Hamirpur is a district town in Himachal Pradesh, known for its education institutions. The Baba Balak Nath temple at Deotsidh and the Sujanpur Tira fort are nearby.',
    'hansi' => 'Hansi is one of the oldest towns in Haryana, with the ruins of Asigarh Fort and the old Barsi Gate. It is easily combined with trips to Hisar.',
    'hanumangarh' => 'Hanumangarh is a district town in northern Rajasthan on the Ghaggar river. The ancient Bhatner Fort, the Harappan site of Kalibangan and the Gogamedi temple are nearby.',
    'hapur' => 'Hapur is a district town in Uttar Pradesh just east of Delhi on NH-9. It is a trading centre and the gateway to Garh Mukteshwar on the Ganga.',
    'hardo-rattan' => 'Hardo Rattan is a small place in Rajasthan. Share your exact location and we will plan the best route and pickup timing for your group.',
    'hardoi' => 'Hardoi is a district town in central Uttar Pradesh, linked in legend with Prahlad and Holika. Prahlad Kund and the Sandi bird sanctuary are local sights.',
    'hasanpur' => 'Hasanpur is a town in Amroha district of western Uttar Pradesh. It is easily combined with trips to Amroha and Gajraula.',
    'hastinapur' => 'Hastinapur near Meerut is the ancient capital of the Kauravas in the Mahabharata. Today it is an important Jain pilgrimage centre with the Jambudweep temple, and also has a wildlife sanctuary along the Ganga.',
    'hatgad' => 'Hatgad is a village in Nashik district of Maharashtra, close to the Saputara hill station on the Gujarat border. The old Hatgad Fort stands nearby. It is a long-distance trip from Delhi.',
    'hathras' => 'Hathras is a district town in Uttar Pradesh between Aligarh and Mathura, known for its asafoetida (hing) and colour trade. The Dau Ji temple is a local landmark.',
    'hemkunt-sahib' => 'Hemkunt Sahib is a high-altitude Sikh shrine at about 4,600 m in Chamoli district, beside a glacial lake. The road ends at Govindghat, from where pilgrims trek via Ghangaria, which is also the base for the Valley of Flowers.',
    'hindaun-city' => 'Hindaun City is a town in Karauli district of Rajasthan. The Shri Mahavirji Jain temple is nearby, and the Kaila Devi temple is a short drive away.',
    'hisar' => 'Hisar is a major city in Haryana, known for its agricultural university and livestock farms. The Agroha Dham temple, Firoz Shah\'s palace and Blue Bird Lake are local attractions.',
    'hodal' => 'Hodal is a town in Palwal district of Haryana on the Delhi–Agra highway. It is a common stop on the way to Mathura and Agra.',
    'hoshiarpur' => 'Hoshiarpur is a city in Punjab at the foot of the Shivalik hills, known for inlay woodwork. It is a gateway to Chintpurni and the Kangra valley.',
    'huzur-nagar' => 'Huzurnagar is a town in Suryapet district of Telangana. Nagarjuna Sagar dam is within driving distance. It is a long-distance trip from Delhi, best done over several days.',
    'iqbalgadh' => 'Iqbalgadh is a small town in Banaskantha district of north Gujarat, between Ambaji and Mount Abu. It is easily combined with trips to both.',
    'jagadhri' => 'Jagadhri is the twin town of Yamuna Nagar in Haryana, known for its metal utensils industry. Adi Badri and the Kalesar National Park are nearby.',
    'jagraon' => 'Jagraon is a town in Ludhiana district of Punjab, known for its grain market. It is easily combined with trips to Ludhiana and Moga.',
    'jaisalmer' => 'Jaisalmer, the "Golden City" of Rajasthan, rises from the Thar Desert around its living sandstone fort. Patwon ki Haveli, Gadisar Lake and camel safaris and desert camps at the Sam Sand Dunes make it a classic Rajasthan trip.',
    'jaitaran' => 'Jaitaran is a town in Pali district of Rajasthan. It is easily combined with trips to Pali, Beawar and Jodhpur.',
    'jalalpur' => 'Jalalpur is a town in Ambedkar Nagar district of eastern Uttar Pradesh. It is best visited as part of a wider trip to Ayodhya or Jaunpur.',
    'jalandhar' => 'Jalandhar is one of Punjab\'s oldest cities, famous for its sports-goods industry. The Devi Talab Mandir, Wonderland theme park and the Pushpa Gujral Science City nearby are popular stops.',
    'jalaun' => 'Jalaun is a district in Uttar Pradesh\'s Bundelkhand region, on the Yamuna. The historic town of Kalpi, birthplace of Ved Vyas by tradition, is nearby.',
    'jalesar' => 'Jalesar is a town in Etah district of Uttar Pradesh, famous for its brass bells (ghungroo and ghanta). It is easily combined with trips to Agra and Etah.',
    'jalore' => 'Jalore is a district town in south-western Rajasthan, known for its hilltop Jalore Fort and granite industry. The Sundha Mata Temple in the Aravallis is nearby.',
    'jammu' => 'Jammu, the "City of Temples", is the winter capital of Jammu and Kashmir. The Raghunath Temple, Bahu Fort and Mubarak Mandi Palace are the highlights, and Katra for Vaishno Devi is about 50 km away.',
    'jaora' => 'Jaora is a town in Ratlam district of Madhya Pradesh. The Hussain Tekri shrine draws large numbers of pilgrims.',
    'jaspur' => 'Jaspur is a town in Udham Singh Nagar district of Uttarakhand near the UP border. It is easily combined with trips to Kashipur and Jim Corbett.',
    'jatipura' => 'Jatipura is a village on the Govardhan Parikrama in Mathura district. It is home to the Mukharvind temple of Shrinathji and is an important stop for Pushti Marg devotees.',
    'jaunpur' => 'Jaunpur in eastern Uttar Pradesh was the capital of the Sharqi sultans, known for its distinctive mosques. The Shahi Qila, the Atala Masjid and the 16th-century Shahi Bridge over the Gomti are the highlights.',
    'jawali' => 'Jawali is a town in Kangra district of Himachal Pradesh, near the Pong Dam lake. It is easily combined with trips to Nurpur and Kangra.',
    'jeolikote' => 'Jeolikote is a quiet village on the Haldwani–Nainital road in Uttarakhand, known for butterflies, birds and orchards. It is a calm base about 18 km before Nainital.',
    'jewar' => 'Jewar is a town in Gautam Buddh Nagar district of Uttar Pradesh on the Yamuna Expressway, where the new Noida International Airport is being built. It is on the route from Delhi to Agra.',
    'jhajjar' => 'Jhajjar is a district town in Haryana west of Delhi. The Bhindawas Bird Sanctuary and the Gurukul archaeological museum are local attractions.',
    'jhalawar' => 'Jhalawar in south-eastern Rajasthan is a green district with lakes and forts. The Gagron water fort (a UNESCO site), Jhalawar Fort and the Chandrabhaga temples are the highlights.',
    'jhanduta' => 'Jhanduta is a small town in Bilaspur district of Himachal Pradesh. It is easily combined with trips to Bilaspur and Ghumarwin.',
    'jhansi' => 'Jhansi in Uttar Pradesh\'s Bundelkhand is forever linked with Rani Lakshmibai. The Jhansi Fort and Rani Mahal are must-sees, and the temple town of Orchha is only 18 km away.',
    'jhunjhunu' => 'Jhunjhunu is the heart of Rajasthan\'s Shekhawati region, known for its painted havelis and the Rani Sati Temple. Khetri Mahal and the havelis of Mandawa and Nawalgarh are nearby.',
    'jim-corbett' => 'Jim Corbett National Park in Uttarakhand is India\'s oldest national park and one of the best places to spot tigers. Jeep safaris in the Dhikala, Bijrani and Jhirna zones, the Garjia Devi Temple and Corbett Falls make it a favourite weekend trip from Delhi.',
    'jind' => 'Jind is a district town in Haryana with strong links to the Mahabharata. The Pandu Pindara tirth and the Jayanti Devi temple are its best-known sites.',
    'jobner' => 'Jobner is a town in Jaipur district of Rajasthan, known for its agriculture college and the hilltop Jwala Mata temple.',
    'joginder-nagar' => 'Joginder Nagar is a town in Mandi district of Himachal Pradesh, known for the Shanan hydel project and its old haulage trolley. Barot valley and Bir Billing are nearby.',
    'jolly-grant' => 'Jolly Grant is home to Dehradun\'s airport, between Dehradun and Rishikesh in Uttarakhand. It is a common pickup and drop point for groups flying in for Rishikesh, Mussoorie or the Char Dham.',
    'joshimath' => 'Joshimath (Jyotirmath) in Chamoli district is a key stop on the way to Badrinath and Hemkund Sahib. It is home to the Narsingh Temple and the Jyotirmath of Adi Shankaracharya, and is the base for Auli.',
    'jubbal' => 'Jubbal is a hill town in Shimla district of Himachal Pradesh, known for the Jubbal Palace and apple orchards. The Hatkoti Durga temple is nearby.',
    'jwalamukhi' => 'Jwalamukhi in Kangra district of Himachal Pradesh is home to the Jwalamukhi Temple, where natural flames burn without any fuel. It is one of the important Shakti Peethas and is often combined with Chintpurni and Kangra.',
    'kadipur' => 'Kadipur is a town in Sultanpur district of eastern Uttar Pradesh. It is easily combined with trips to Sultanpur and Ayodhya.',
    'kaithal' => 'Kaithal is a district town in Haryana with ancient temples and tanks. The Gyarah Rudri Shiv Temple and Bidkiyar Lake are its main sights.',
    'kala-amb' => 'Kala Amb is an industrial town in Sirmaur district of Himachal Pradesh, near the Haryana border. Nahan and Renuka Ji are a short drive away.',
    'kalka' => 'Kalka is a town in Panchkula district of Haryana at the foot of the Shivalik hills. It is the starting point of the UNESCO-listed Kalka–Shimla toy train, and Pinjore Gardens are next door.',
    'kaloli-rajasthan' => 'Kaloli is a small place in Rajasthan. Share your exact location and we will plan the best route and pickup timing for your group.',
    'kalpa' => 'Kalpa is a beautiful village in Kinnaur district of Himachal Pradesh, facing the sacred Kinner Kailash range. Apple orchards, old temples and nearby Roghi village make it a highlight of a Kinnaur–Spiti trip.',
    'kalyanpur' => 'Kalyanpur is a locality in Kanpur, Uttar Pradesh, near IIT Kanpur. It is a convenient pickup and drop point in the city.',
    'kanatal' => 'Kanatal is a quiet hill getaway in Tehri Garhwal, Uttarakhand, on the Chamba–Mussoorie road. It is known for camping, the Kodia jungle, the Surkanda Devi Temple and views over Tehri Lake.',
    'kandaghat' => 'Kandaghat is a small town in Solan district of Himachal Pradesh on the Kalka–Shimla highway. It is the turn-off for Chail.',
    'kangra' => 'Kangra is a historic town in Himachal Pradesh, known for the massive Kangra Fort and Kangra miniature paintings. The Brajeshwari Devi temple and the Masroor rock-cut temples are nearby.',
    'kanhe-phata' => 'Kanhe Phata is a small place in Maharashtra. It is a long-distance trip from Delhi; share your exact location and we will plan the route and halts.',
    'kannauj' => 'Kannauj is an ancient city in Uttar Pradesh, famous as India\'s perfume capital, where attar is still distilled in traditional copper stills.',
    'kanpur' => 'Kanpur is one of Uttar Pradesh\'s biggest cities, known for its leather and textile industries. The JK Temple, Allen Forest Zoo and Moti Jheel are local sights, and Bithoor on the Ganga is nearby.',
    'kanth' => 'Kanth is a town in Moradabad district of Uttar Pradesh. It is easily combined with trips to Moradabad.',
    'kapkot' => 'Kapkot is a town in Bageshwar district of Uttarakhand on the Saryu river. It is the road head for the Pindari and Sunderdhunga glacier treks.',
    'kapurthala' => 'Kapurthala is a former princely state in Punjab, known as the "Paris of Punjab" for its French-style Jagatjit Palace. The Moorish Mosque and the Pushpa Gujral Science City are nearby.',
    'karauli' => 'Karauli is a heritage town in eastern Rajasthan, known for its red sandstone. The Kaila Devi Temple, the City Palace and the Madan Mohan Ji temple are the highlights.',
    'karnal' => 'Karnal is a city in Haryana on the GT Road, named after Karna of the Mahabharata. Karna Lake and the Kalpana Chawla Planetarium are local stops.',
    'karnaprayag' => 'Karnaprayag in Chamoli district is where the Alaknanda meets the Pindar river. It is one of the five sacred prayags on the Badrinath route.',
    'kasauli' => 'Kasauli is a peaceful colonial hill station in Solan district of Himachal Pradesh. Christ Church, the Mall, the Gilbert Trail, Monkey Point and sunset views make it a favourite weekend getaway from Delhi.',
    'kasganj' => 'Kasganj is a district town in western Uttar Pradesh. The holy town of Soron (Shukar Kshetra), linked with Tulsidas, is nearby.',
    'kashipur-uttarakhand' => 'Kashipur is a city in Udham Singh Nagar district of Uttarakhand. The Chaiti Devi temple, linked with the Chaiti fair, and the ancient Drona Sagar are local sights, and Jim Corbett is close by.',
    'kasol' => 'Kasol in the Parvati Valley of Himachal Pradesh is a riverside village loved by backpackers. Manikaran Sahib, the Kheerganga trek and the villages of Tosh and Malana are nearby.',
    'kathgodam' => 'Kathgodam in Uttarakhand is the last railway station before the Kumaon hills, next to Haldwani. Most trips to Nainital, Bhimtal and Almora pass through here.',
    'katni' => 'Katni is a railway junction city in Madhya Pradesh, known for its limestone industry. It is a stop on the way to Bandhavgarh National Park. It is a long trip from Delhi.',
    'katra' => 'Katra in Jammu and Kashmir is the base town for the Mata Vaishno Devi yatra. Pilgrims register here and begin the 12 km trek to the Bhawan, and the Bhimgarh Fort overlooks the town.',
    'kausani' => 'Kausani in Bageshwar district of Uttarakhand offers one of the widest views of the Himalaya, a 300 km sweep from Trishul to Panchachuli. Mahatma Gandhi called it the "Switzerland of India"; the Anasakti Ashram and tea estate are nearby.',
    'kaza' => 'Kaza is the main town of the Spiti Valley in Himachal Pradesh, a cold desert at about 3,800 m. Key Monastery, Kibber, Langza, Hikkim (the world\'s highest post office) and Chandratal make it a trip of a lifetime.',
    'kedarnath' => 'Kedarnath is one of the twelve Jyotirlingas and one of the Char Dham shrines, set at about 3,580 m in Rudraprayag district. The road ends at Gaurikund, from where pilgrims trek about 16 km to the temple; we drop and pick up at Sonprayag or Gaurikund.',
    'kekri' => 'Kekri is a town in Ajmer district of Rajasthan. It is easily combined with trips to Ajmer and Pushkar.',
    'keylong' => 'Keylong is the headquarters of Lahaul in Himachal Pradesh, just beyond the Atal Tunnel. The Kardang and Shashur monasteries and Sissu are nearby, and it is a key halt on the Manali–Leh highway.',
    'khairthal' => 'Khairthal is a town in Rajasthan near Alwar, known for its grain market. It is easily combined with trips to Alwar.',
    'khajjiar' => 'Khajjiar near Dalhousie in Himachal Pradesh is called the "Mini Switzerland of India" for its meadow ringed by deodar forest. The Khajji Nag temple and the Kalatop sanctuary are nearby.',
    'khajuraho' => 'Khajuraho in Madhya Pradesh is famous for its UNESCO-listed Chandela temples with exquisite carvings. Panna National Park and the Raneh Falls canyon are nearby.',
    'khandela' => 'Khandela is a historic town in Sikar district of Rajasthan\'s Shekhawati region, known for its old forts and havelis.',
    'khanna' => 'Khanna is a town in Ludhiana district of Punjab on the GT Road, known for one of Asia\'s largest grain markets.',
    'kharar' => 'Kharar is a fast-growing town in Mohali district of Punjab, on the Chandigarh–Ropar road. Chandigarh is about 15 km away.',
    'khatauli' => 'Khatauli is a town in Muzaffarnagar district of Uttar Pradesh on the Delhi–Haridwar highway. It is a common highway stop on the way to Haridwar.',
    'khatima' => 'Khatima is a town in Udham Singh Nagar district of Uttarakhand near the Nepal border. The Nanakmatta Sahib gurdwara and the Sharda barrage are nearby.',
    'khatu-shyam' => 'Khatu Shyam in Rajasthan\'s Sikar district is home to the famous Khatu Shyam Ji Temple, dedicated to Barbarik. Lakhs of devotees visit during the Phalgun mela, and Salasar Balaji is often added to the same trip.',
    'khetri' => 'Khetri is a historic town in Jhunjhunu district of Rajasthan, linked with Swami Vivekananda. The Khetri Mahal (wind palace) and Bhopalgarh Fort are its main sights.',
    'khijuriwas' => 'Khijuriwas is a small place in Haryana. Share your exact location and we will plan the best route and pickup timing for your group.',
    'khimsar' => 'Khimsar is a village in Nagaur district of Rajasthan, known for the Khimsar Fort heritage hotel and its sand dunes. It is a peaceful desert stay between Jodhpur and Nagaur.',
    'khurja' => 'Khurja in Bulandshahr district of Uttar Pradesh is India\'s well-known pottery town, with shops selling ceramic crockery and decor.',
    'kichha' => 'Kichha is a town in Udham Singh Nagar district of Uttarakhand, between Rudrapur and Bareilly. It is easily combined with trips to the Kumaon hills.',
    'kinnaur' => 'Kinnaur in Himachal Pradesh is a dramatic valley along the Sutlej, with Reckong Peo as its headquarters. Kalpa, Sangla, Chitkul (the last village on the Indo-Tibet road) and Nako are the highlights.',
    'kiratpur-sahib' => 'Kiratpur Sahib is a holy Sikh town in Rupnagar district of Punjab on the Sutlej. Gurdwara Patalpuri Sahib is here, and Anandpur Sahib is just 10 km away.',
    'kishangarh' => 'Kishangarh in Rajasthan is famous for its Bani Thani miniature paintings and its marble market. The Kishangarh Fort and the white "marble dumping yard" are popular photo spots.',
    'kosi-kalan' => 'Kosi Kalan is a town in Mathura district of Uttar Pradesh on the Delhi–Agra highway. The Shani Dev temple at Kokilavan is nearby.',
    'kosli' => 'Kosli is a town in Rewari district of Haryana. It is easily combined with trips to Rewari and Jhajjar.',
    'kota' => 'Kota in Rajasthan is famous as India\'s coaching hub and for the Chambal river. The Garh Palace, Kishore Sagar, the Seven Wonders Park and the Chambal Riverfront are its highlights.',
    'kotdwara' => 'Kotdwar (Kotdwara) is the gateway to the Garhwal hills of Uttarakhand and to Lansdowne. The Siddhbali Temple and Kanvashram, linked with Shakuntala, are nearby.',
    'kotkapura' => 'Kotkapura is a town in Faridkot district of Punjab. It is easily combined with trips to Faridkot and Bathinda.',
    'kotputli' => 'Kotputli is a town in Rajasthan on the Delhi–Jaipur highway. It is a common highway halt on the way to Jaipur.',
    'kuchaman-city' => 'Kuchaman City in Rajasthan\'s Nagaur district is known for the hilltop Kuchaman Fort, now a heritage hotel. Sambhar Lake is nearby.',
    'kufri' => 'Kufri is a small hill resort near Shimla, Himachal Pradesh, known for snow in winter, yak rides and pony rides. Kufri Fun World, the Himalayan Nature Park and Mahasu Peak are its highlights.',
    'kukas' => 'Kukas is on the Delhi–Jaipur highway just north of Jaipur, close to Amber Fort. It is known for its resorts and wedding venues.',
    'kullu' => 'Kullu is a valley town on the Beas river in Himachal Pradesh, known for the Raghunath Temple, river rafting and the famous Kullu Dussehra. Bijli Mahadev and Manali are close by.',
    'kumbhalgarh' => 'Kumbhalgarh in Rajasthan\'s Rajsamand district is home to Kumbhalgarh Fort, a UNESCO site whose wall is among the longest in the world. The Kumbhalgarh Wildlife Sanctuary and the evening light-and-sound show are highlights.',
    'kundarki' => 'Kundarki is a town in Moradabad district of Uttar Pradesh. It is easily combined with trips to Moradabad.',
    'kurebhar' => 'Kurebhar is a small town in Sultanpur district of eastern Uttar Pradesh. It is best visited as part of a wider trip to Sultanpur or Ayodhya.',
    'kurukshetra' => 'Kurukshetra in Haryana is the land of the Mahabharata war and the Bhagavad Gita. Brahma Sarovar, Jyotisar, the Sri Krishna Museum and Sannihit Sarovar are its main sights.',
    'lachhipura' => 'Lachhipura is a small place in Rajasthan. Share your exact location and we will plan the best route and pickup timing for your group.',
    'ladnun' => 'Ladnun is a town in Nagaur district of Rajasthan, home to the Jain Vishva Bharati Institute of the Terapanth sect.',
    'laharpur' => 'Laharpur is a town in Sitapur district of Uttar Pradesh. It is easily combined with trips to Sitapur and Naimisharanya.',
    'lakhimpur' => 'Lakhimpur Kheri is the largest district in Uttar Pradesh, on the Nepal border. It is the gateway to Dudhwa National Park, and the unique Frog Temple at Oel is nearby.',
    'laksar' => 'Laksar is a town in Haridwar district of Uttarakhand and a railway junction. Haridwar is a short drive away.',
    'lalkuan' => 'Lalkuan is a town in Nainital district of Uttarakhand, near Haldwani. It is on the route to Nainital and the Kumaon hills.',
    'lalru' => 'Lalru is a town in Mohali district of Punjab on the Ambala–Chandigarh highway. It is easily combined with trips to Chandigarh and Zirakpur.',
    'lansdowne' => 'Lansdowne in Pauri Garhwal is a quiet cantonment hill station and home of the Garhwal Rifles. Tip-n-Top, Bhulla Tal, St Mary\'s Church and the Tarkeshwar Mahadev temple make it a peaceful weekend escape from Delhi.',
    'laxmangarh' => 'Laxmangarh in Rajasthan\'s Sikar district is known for its hilltop fort and some of the finest painted havelis of Shekhawati.',
    'loharu' => 'Loharu is a town in Bhiwani district of Haryana near the Rajasthan border, once a small princely state. It is easily combined with trips to Pilani and Bhiwani.',
    'loni' => 'Loni is a town in Ghaziabad district of Uttar Pradesh on Delhi\'s north-eastern border. It is a common pickup point for trips starting from east Delhi.',
    'ludhiana' => 'Ludhiana is Punjab\'s largest city and an industrial hub, known for hosiery and bicycles. The Lodhi Fort, the PAU museum and the Tiger Safari are local attractions.',
    'madhopur-punjab' => 'Madhopur is a town in Pathankot district of Punjab, known for the Madhopur headworks on the Ravi. It lies on the route to Jammu and the hills of Himachal.',
    'mahendragarh' => 'Mahendragarh is a district town in southern Haryana. The old Madhogarh Fort on a nearby hill is the main sight.',
    'mahoba' => 'Mahoba in Uttar Pradesh\'s Bundelkhand was a Chandela capital, known for its lakes, temples and the legends of Alha and Udal. Kirat Sagar and Gorakhgiri hill are the highlights.',
    'mainpuri' => 'Mainpuri is a district town in western Uttar Pradesh. It is easily combined with trips to Etawah and Agra.',
    'makhu' => 'Makhu is a town in Ferozepur district of Punjab. The Harike wetland bird sanctuary is nearby.',
    'maksi' => 'Maksi is a town in Shajapur district of Madhya Pradesh. It is close to Ujjain and its Mahakaleshwar temple.',
    'malerkotla' => 'Malerkotla is a historic town in Punjab, once a princely state. The Dargah of Haider Shaikh and the Mubarak Manzil Palace are its best-known sights.',
    'malout' => 'Malout is a town in Sri Muktsar Sahib district of Punjab. It is easily combined with trips to Muktsar and Abohar.',
    'malpura' => 'Malpura is a town in Tonk district of Rajasthan. It is easily combined with trips to Tonk and Ajmer.',
    'mandav' => 'Mandu (Mandav) in Madhya Pradesh is a ruined hilltop city full of Afghan architecture. The Jahaz Mahal, Rani Roopmati\'s Pavilion and Baz Bahadur\'s Palace are especially beautiful in the monsoon.',
    'mandawa' => 'Mandawa is the best-known town of Rajasthan\'s Shekhawati region, often called an open-air art gallery for its frescoed havelis. The Mandawa Castle is now a heritage hotel.',
    'mandi' => 'Mandi is a temple town on the Beas in Himachal Pradesh, called the "Varanasi of the Hills". The Bhootnath Temple, Rewalsar Lake and Prashar Lake are nearby, and it is a key stop on the Manali highway.',
    'mandi-gobindgarh-punjab' => 'Mandi Gobindgarh in Punjab is called the "Steel Town of India" for its many rolling mills. Fatehgarh Sahib is nearby.',
    'mandsaur' => 'Mandsaur in Madhya Pradesh is known for the Pashupatinath Temple on the Shivna river, with its rare eight-faced Shiva idol. The Gandhi Sagar Dam is nearby.',
    'manesar' => 'Manesar is an industrial town in Gurugram district of Haryana, home to many auto companies. Damdama Lake and the Sultanpur Bird Sanctuary are nearby.',
    'manikaran' => 'Manikaran in the Parvati Valley of Himachal Pradesh is famous for its hot springs and the Manikaran Sahib Gurdwara, where langar is cooked in the hot water. Kasol is just 5 km away.',
    'mansa' => 'Mansa is a district town in Punjab\'s Malwa region. It is easily combined with trips to Bathinda and Sangrur.',
    'marwar-bhinmal' => 'Bhinmal in Rajasthan\'s Jalore district is an ancient town, once a capital of the Gurjara kingdom. The Varah Shyam temple and several Jain temples are its main sights.',
    'marwar-ranawas' => 'Ranawas is a small town in Pali district of Rajasthan, on the Jodhpur–Pali route. It is easily combined with trips to Pali and Jodhpur.',
    'mashobra' => 'Mashobra is a quiet hill village near Shimla, Himachal Pradesh, known for apple orchards and pine forests. Craignano Nature Park and the Shali Tibba trek are nearby.',
    'mathura' => 'Mathura is the birthplace of Lord Krishna and the heart of the Braj region. Shri Krishna Janmabhoomi, the Dwarkadhish Temple and Vishram Ghat on the Yamuna are the highlights, with Vrindavan just 12 km away.',
    'mayapur' => 'Mayapur in West Bengal is the world headquarters of ISKCON and the birthplace of Chaitanya Mahaprabhu. The huge Temple of the Vedic Planetarium and the Chandrodaya Mandir draw devotees from across the world. It is a long-distance trip from Delhi.',
    'mcleod-ganj' => 'McLeod Ganj above Dharamshala is the home of the Dalai Lama and the Tibetan government-in-exile, often called "Little Lhasa". The Tsuglagkhang complex, Bhagsu Falls, Naddi viewpoint and the Triund trek are the highlights.',
    'medhupur' => 'Medhupur is a small place in Uttar Pradesh. Share your exact location and we will plan the best route and pickup timing for your group.',
    'meerut' => 'Meerut is a historic city in Uttar Pradesh where the 1857 uprising began. The Augarnath Temple, St John\'s Church and the nearby Hastinapur make it a short trip from Delhi.',
    'mehandipur-balaji' => 'Mehandipur Balaji in Rajasthan\'s Dausa district is a famous Hanuman temple known for faith healing. Devotees from across north India visit the Balaji, Pret Raj and Bhairav shrines.',
    'mehrauli' => 'Mehrauli in south Delhi is one of the city\'s oldest areas. The Qutub Minar, the Mehrauli Archaeological Park and many old monuments and tombs make it a good local heritage outing.',
    'merta' => 'Merta in Rajasthan\'s Nagaur district is the birthplace of the poet-saint Meera Bai. The Meera Bai temple and the Charbhuja Nath temple are its main sights.',
    'mhow' => 'Mhow (Dr Ambedkar Nagar) is a cantonment town near Indore in Madhya Pradesh, the birthplace of Dr B. R. Ambedkar. Patalpani waterfall and Janapav hill are nearby.',
    'milak' => 'Milak is a town in Rampur district of Uttar Pradesh. It is easily combined with trips to Rampur and Bareilly.',
    'mirthal' => 'Mirthal is a small place in Pathankot district of Punjab. It is easily combined with trips to Pathankot.',
    'mirzapur' => 'Mirzapur in Uttar Pradesh is known for its carpets, its ghats on the Ganga and the Vindhyachal Devi temple. The Chunar Fort and the waterfalls of the Vindhya hills are nearby.',
    'misrikh-cum-neemsar' => 'Misrikh (with Neemsar, Naimisharanya) in Sitapur district is one of the holiest places in Hinduism, where sage Dadhichi is said to have given his bones. Dadhichi Kund, Chakra Tirth and the Lalita Devi temple are the main sights.',
    'modinagar' => 'Modinagar is an industrial town in Ghaziabad district of Uttar Pradesh on the Delhi–Meerut road. It is easily combined with trips to Meerut.',
    'moga' => 'Moga is a district town in Punjab\'s Malwa region. It is easily combined with trips to Ludhiana and Ferozepur.',
    'mohali' => 'Mohali (SAS Nagar) is Chandigarh\'s twin city in Punjab, home to the PCA cricket stadium and Chandigarh\'s international airport. Gurdwara Amb Sahib is a local landmark.',
    'moonak' => 'Moonak is a town in Sangrur district of Punjab. It is easily combined with trips to Sangrur and Patiala.',
    'moradabad' => 'Moradabad in Uttar Pradesh is known worldwide as the "Brass City" for its brassware exports. It lies on NH-9, the main route from Delhi to Nainital and the Kumaon hills.',
    'morena' => 'Morena in Madhya Pradesh sits in the Chambal region. The restored Bateshwar temple group, the Mitawali circular temple and the National Chambal Sanctuary are nearby.',
    'morinda' => 'Morinda is a town in Rupnagar district of Punjab. Gurdwara Kotwali Sahib is linked with the history of the younger Sahibzadas.',
    'morni-hills' => 'Morni Hills in Panchkula district is Haryana\'s only hill station. Tikkar Tal lakes, the old Morni Fort and an adventure park make it a quick getaway from Chandigarh.',
    'mount-abu' => 'Mount Abu is Rajasthan\'s only hill station, set in the Aravallis. The marble Dilwara Jain temples, Nakki Lake, Guru Shikhar and Sunset Point are the highlights.',
    'mukerian' => 'Mukerian is a town in Hoshiarpur district of Punjab on the Jalandhar–Pathankot highway. It is easily combined with trips to Pathankot and Talwara.',
    'mukteshwar' => 'Mukteshwar in Nainital district of Uttarakhand is a quiet hill station with Himalayan views. The Mukteshwar Dham temple, the cliffs of Chauli ki Jali and the old IVRI campus are the highlights.',
    'muktsar' => 'Sri Muktsar Sahib in Punjab is a holy Sikh city linked with the Forty Liberated Ones (Chali Mukte). The Gurdwara Tuti Gandhi Sahib and the Maghi Mela draw large crowds.',
    'mukundgarh' => 'Mukundgarh in Rajasthan\'s Shekhawati region is known for its fort, now a heritage hotel, and its painted havelis and handicrafts.',
    'mullana' => 'Mullana is a town in Ambala district of Haryana, home to a large university campus. It is easily combined with trips to Ambala.',
    'munsiyari' => 'Munsiyari in Pithoragarh district of Uttarakhand sits right in front of the Panchachuli peaks. Khaliya Top, Birthi Falls and the Nanda Devi temple make it a favourite with trekkers and photographers.',
    'murthal' => 'Murthal in Sonipat district of Haryana is famous for its 24-hour dhabas and stuffed parathas on the GT Road. It is a popular food stop right out of Delhi.',
    'musafirkhana' => 'Musafirkhana is a town in Amethi district of Uttar Pradesh. It is easily combined with trips to Sultanpur and Amethi.',
    'muzaffarnagar' => 'Muzaffarnagar is a city in western Uttar Pradesh on the Delhi–Haridwar highway, known for its sugar and jaggery. Shukratal on the Ganga is nearby.',
    'nabha' => 'Nabha is a former princely state in Punjab\'s Patiala district. The Nabha Fort and the Hira Mahal are its heritage sights.',
    'nagaur' => 'Nagaur in Rajasthan is known for the Ahhichatragarh Fort and its famous winter cattle fair. Khimsar and its dunes are nearby.',
    'nagina' => 'Nagina in Bijnor district of Uttar Pradesh is known for its fine wood-carving craft.',
    'nagrota-surian' => 'Nagrota Surian in Kangra district of Himachal Pradesh lies beside the Pong Dam lake, a major wintering spot for migratory birds.',
    'nahan' => 'Nahan is the district headquarters of Sirmaur in Himachal Pradesh, a neat hill town built around Rani Tal. The Jaitak Fort and Renuka Lake are nearby.',
    'naimisaradya' => 'Naimisharanya (Neemsar) in Sitapur district of Uttar Pradesh is an ancient sacred forest where the Puranas are said to have been narrated. Chakra Tirth, Vyas Gaddi and the Lalita Devi temple are the main sights.',
    'naina-devi' => 'Naina Devi in Bilaspur district of Himachal Pradesh is home to the Shri Naina Devi Temple, a Shakti Peetha on a hilltop overlooking the Gobind Sagar lake. A ropeway leads up to the temple.',
    'najibabad' => 'Najibabad is a town in Bijnor district of Uttar Pradesh, founded by Najib-ud-Daula. The Pathargarh Fort is its main historical site.',
    'nakodar-punjab' => 'Nakodar is a town in Jalandhar district of Punjab, known for the Dera Baba Murad Shah shrine.',
    'nalagarh' => 'Nalagarh is a town in Solan district of Himachal Pradesh. The old Nalagarh Fort, now a heritage resort, overlooks the town.',
    'naldehra' => 'Naldehra near Shimla in Himachal Pradesh is known for its scenic golf course among deodar forests. The Mahunag temple and the Tattapani hot springs are nearby.',
    'nanak-jhira-sahib' => 'Gurdwara Nanak Jhira Sahib in Bidar, Karnataka, marks the spot where Guru Nanak Dev Ji is said to have brought forth a spring. The Bidar Fort is nearby. It is a long-distance trip from Delhi, best planned over several days.',
    'nangal' => 'Nangal in Punjab\'s Rupnagar district is next to the Bhakra Nangal dam. Nangal Lake and the dam viewpoints are its main attractions.',
    'naraingarh' => 'Naraingarh is a town in Ambala district of Haryana at the foot of the Shivaliks. Morni Hills are nearby.',
    'narkanda' => 'Narkanda is a hill station in Shimla district of Himachal Pradesh, known for skiing in winter and apple orchards. Hatu Peak and Tannu Jubbar Lake are the highlights.',
    'narnaul' => 'Narnaul in southern Haryana has many Mughal-era monuments, including the Jal Mahal and Chor Gumbad. The Dhosi Hill, linked with sage Chyavan, is nearby.',
    'narora' => 'Narora is a town on the Ganga in Bulandshahr district of Uttar Pradesh, known for its atomic power station and Ganga barrage. Raj Ghat is a popular bathing ghat.',
    'narwana' => 'Narwana is a town in Jind district of Haryana. It is easily combined with trips to Jind and Kaithal.',
    'nathdwara' => 'Nathdwara near Udaipur is home to the Shrinathji Temple, one of the most important Krishna shrines. The giant Statue of Belief (Vishwas Swaroopam) and Haldighati are nearby.',
    'national-chambal-wildlife-sanctuary' => 'The National Chambal Sanctuary protects the Chambal river across Madhya Pradesh, Rajasthan and Uttar Pradesh. Boat safaris show gharials, crocodiles, Gangetic dolphins and river birds amid dramatic ravines.',
    'naukuchiatal' => 'Naukuchiatal near Bhimtal in Uttarakhand is a lake with nine corners. It is known for paragliding, boating and birdwatching.',
    'nawalgarh' => 'Nawalgarh in Rajasthan\'s Shekhawati region is known for its painted havelis. The Poddar Haveli Museum and the Morarka Haveli are highlights.',
    'nawanshahr' => 'Nawanshahr (Shaheed Bhagat Singh Nagar) is a district town in Punjab. The ancestral village of Bhagat Singh at Khatkar Kalan, with its museum, is nearby.',
    'naya-nangal' => 'Naya Nangal is a township next to Nangal in Punjab, close to the Bhakra Dam.',
    'neemrana' => 'Neemrana in Rajasthan is famous for the 15th-century Neemrana Fort Palace, now a heritage hotel, and its zipline. It is one of the easiest weekend getaways from Delhi.',
    'neemuch' => 'Neemuch is a district town in Madhya Pradesh near the Rajasthan border. The Gandhi Sagar Dam and the Bhadwa Mata temple are nearby.',
    'nilokheri' => 'Nilokheri is a town in Karnal district of Haryana on the GT Road. It is easily combined with trips to Karnal and Kurukshetra.',
    'nohar' => 'Nohar is a town in Hanumangarh district of northern Rajasthan. It is easily combined with trips to Hanumangarh and Sirsa.',
    'noida' => 'Noida is a planned city in Uttar Pradesh right next to Delhi and one of the busiest pickup points for our trips. Worlds of Wonder, the Botanical Garden, DLF Mall of India and Okhla Bird Sanctuary are local attractions.',
    'nokha' => 'Nokha is a town in Bikaner district of Rajasthan. It is easily combined with trips to Bikaner and Deshnoke.',
    'nowrangpur' => 'Nabarangpur is a district town in southern Odisha, in a tribal, forested region. It is a long-distance trip from Delhi, best planned over several days.',
    'nuh' => 'Nuh is a district town in Haryana\'s Mewat region. The Sheikh Musa Dargah and Kotla Lake are local sights.',
    'nurpur' => 'Nurpur in Kangra district of Himachal Pradesh is known for the ruins of Nurpur Fort and the Brij Raj Swami temple inside it. It is the gateway to Dalhousie and Chamba from Pathankot.',
    'orai' => 'Orai is the district headquarters of Jalaun in Uttar Pradesh\'s Bundelkhand region. The historic town of Kalpi on the Yamuna is nearby.',
    'orchha' => 'Orchha in Madhya Pradesh is a beautiful medieval town on the Betwa river. The Ram Raja Temple, Orchha Fort, Jahangir Mahal and the riverside chhatris are the highlights.',
    'osian' => 'Osian near Jodhpur is known as the "Khajuraho of Rajasthan" for its ancient temples. The Sachiya Mata temple, Jain temples and desert camps among the dunes are the highlights.',
    'pahalgam' => 'Pahalgam in Jammu and Kashmir is a stunning valley on the Lidder river. Betaab Valley, Aru Valley, Baisaran meadow and Chandanwari (base of the Amarnath Yatra) are the highlights.',
    'palampur' => 'Palampur in Kangra district of Himachal Pradesh is known for its tea gardens and Dhauladhar views. The Baijnath Temple, Andretta artists\' village and Bir Billing are nearby.',
    'palanpur-gujrat' => 'Palanpur is a district town in north Gujarat, once a princely state. The Balaram Palace and the Jessore sloth bear sanctuary are nearby, and it is the gateway to Ambaji and Mount Abu.',
    'pali' => 'Pali in Rajasthan is a textile town between Jodhpur and Udaipur. The Om Banna "Bullet Baba" shrine, Jawai Dam and Ranakpur are nearby.',
    'palia-kalan' => 'Palia Kalan is a town in Lakhimpur Kheri district of Uttar Pradesh. It is the nearest town to Dudhwa National Park.',
    'palwal' => 'Palwal is a district town in Haryana on the Delhi–Agra highway (NH-19). It is a common stop on the way to Mathura and Agra.',
    'panchkula' => 'Panchkula is a planned city in Haryana next to Chandigarh. The Mansa Devi Temple, Cactus Garden and Pinjore Gardens are popular sights.',
    'panipat' => 'Panipat in Haryana is the site of three historic battles and a major textile hub known for blankets and rugs. The Panipat Museum and Ibrahim Lodhi\'s tomb are its landmarks.',
    'panna' => 'Panna in Madhya Pradesh is known for its diamond mines and Panna National Park, a tiger reserve along the Ken river. Pandav Falls and the Jugal Kishore temple are nearby.',
    'pantnagar' => 'Pantnagar in Uttarakhand is home to the G. B. Pant agricultural university and an airport serving the Kumaon region. It is a common pickup point for Nainital trips.',
    'paonta-sahib-himachal-pradesh' => 'Paonta Sahib in Sirmaur district of Himachal Pradesh is a holy Sikh town on the Yamuna, where Guru Gobind Singh Ji lived and wrote. The Gurdwara Paonta Sahib is the main attraction.',
    'parwanoo' => 'Parwanoo is the first town in Himachal Pradesh on the Kalka–Shimla road. The Timber Trail cable car and fruit-processing units are known here, and Kasauli is nearby.',
    'pataunda' => 'Pataunda is a small place in Uttar Pradesh. Share your exact location and we will plan the best route and pickup timing for your group.',
    'pathankot' => 'Pathankot in Punjab is the meeting point of Punjab, Himachal and Jammu and Kashmir. It is the gateway to Dalhousie, Dharamshala and Jammu.',
    'patiala' => 'Patiala, the royal city of Punjab, is known for its Qila Mubarak, Sheesh Mahal, Patiala peg, Patiala salwar and jutti. Gurdwara Dukh Niwaran Sahib is the main gurdwara.',
    'patnitop' => 'Patnitop is a hill resort in Jammu and Kashmir on the Jammu–Srinagar route, set among deodar forests. Nathatop, Sanasar and Kud are nearby.',
    'pauri-garhwal' => 'Pauri is the headquarters of Pauri Garhwal district in Uttarakhand, with a wide view of the Himalayan peaks. The Kandoliya temple and the nearby Khirsu are its highlights.',
    'pavagarh' => 'Pavagadh in Gujarat is a hill crowned by the Kalika Mata Temple, one of the Shakti Peethas. The Champaner-Pavagadh Archaeological Park around it is a UNESCO World Heritage Site.',
    'pehowa' => 'Pehowa near Kurukshetra in Haryana is an ancient pilgrimage town on the Saraswati. The Prithudak Tirth is known for ancestral rites (pind daan).',
    'phagwara' => 'Phagwara is a city in Kapurthala district of Punjab on the GT Road, home to a large university campus. It is easily combined with trips to Jalandhar.',
    'phalodi' => 'Phalodi in Rajasthan\'s Jodhpur district is known for the nearby village of Khichan, where thousands of demoiselle cranes spend the winter. The Lal Niwas haveli is a local landmark.',
    'phaphund' => 'Phaphund is a town in Auraiya district of Uttar Pradesh, known for its old dargah. It is easily combined with trips to Etawah.',
    'phillaur' => 'Phillaur in Punjab\'s Jalandhar district is known for the Phillaur Fort, now home to the Punjab Police Academy. It lies on the GT Road beside the Sutlej.',
    'pilani' => 'Pilani in Rajasthan is known for BITS Pilani and the Birla family. The Birla Museum and the Saraswati Temple are its main sights.',
    'pilibhit' => 'Pilibhit in Uttar Pradesh is known for the Pilibhit Tiger Reserve and the Chuka beach on the Sharda reservoir.',
    'pinjore' => 'Pinjore near Chandigarh is famous for the Mughal-style Yadavindra (Pinjore) Gardens. The ancient Bhima Devi temple ruins are nearby.',
    'pithoragarh' => 'Pithoragarh in Uttarakhand is a scenic Kumaon town near the Nepal border, sometimes called "Little Kashmir". The Pithoragarh Fort, Chandak hill and the Patal Bhuvaneshwar cave temple are nearby.',
    'pokhran' => 'Pokhran in Rajasthan\'s Jaisalmer district is known for India\'s nuclear tests and its old red-sandstone fort. The Ramdevra temple is just 12 km away.',
    'pratapgarh-rajasthan' => 'Pratapgarh in southern Rajasthan is known for the Thewa art of gold on glass. The Sita Mata Wildlife Sanctuary and the old capital of Deolia are nearby.',
    'pratapgarh-uttar-pradesh' => 'Pratapgarh in Uttar Pradesh is known for its amla (Indian gooseberry) products. The Bhakti Dham at Mangarh and the Belha Devi temple are local sights.',
    'prayagraj' => 'Prayagraj (Allahabad) in Uttar Pradesh is home to the Triveni Sangam, where the Ganga, Yamuna and mythical Saraswati meet, and hosts the Kumbh Mela. Anand Bhavan, the Allahabad Fort and Khusro Bagh are other highlights.',
    'prempura' => 'Prempura is a small place in Rajasthan. Share your exact location and we will plan the best route and pickup timing for your group.',
    'puranpur' => 'Puranpur is a town in Pilibhit district of Uttar Pradesh, close to the Pilibhit Tiger Reserve.',
    'pushkar' => 'Pushkar near Ajmer is one of the holiest towns in India, home to the rare Brahma Temple and the sacred Pushkar Lake with 52 ghats. The Pushkar Camel Fair in October–November is world-famous.',
    'raebareli' => 'Raebareli is a district town in central Uttar Pradesh. The Samaspur Bird Sanctuary and Indira Garden are local attractions.',
    'raichak' => 'Raichak is a riverside getaway on the Hooghly in South 24 Parganas, West Bengal, known for its fort-style resort. It is a long-distance trip from Delhi, best planned over several days.',
    'raigarh' => 'Raigarh is an industrial city in Chhattisgarh, known for Kathak traditions and the Ram Jharna and Singhanpur cave paintings nearby. It is a long-distance trip from Delhi.',
    'raikot' => 'Raikot is a town in Ludhiana district of Punjab. The Gurdwara Tahliana Sahib, linked with Guru Gobind Singh Ji, is its main shrine.',
    'rajaji-national-park' => 'Rajaji National Park spreads across the Shivalik hills near Haridwar and Rishikesh in Uttarakhand. It is known for elephants, leopards and jeep safaris in the Chilla and Motichur ranges.',
    'rajakhera' => 'Rajakhera is a town in Dholpur district of Rajasthan near the Chambal. It is easily combined with trips to Dholpur and Agra.',
    'rajapur-road' => 'Rajapur in Chitrakoot district of Uttar Pradesh is revered as the birthplace of Goswami Tulsidas. Chitrakoot is nearby.',
    'rajpura' => 'Rajpura is a town in Patiala district of Punjab, at the junction of the Ambala–Ludhiana and Patiala roads. It is easily combined with trips to Patiala and Chandigarh.',
    'rajsamand' => 'Rajsamand in Rajasthan is known for its huge Rajsamand Lake and the carved marble pavilions of Nau Chowki. Kumbhalgarh and Nathdwara are nearby.',
    'ram-gaon' => 'Ramgaon is a small place in Uttar Pradesh. Share your exact location and we will plan the best route and pickup timing for your group.',
    'ramdevra' => 'Ramdevra (Runicha) near Pokhran in Rajasthan is home to the Baba Ramdev samadhi temple, which draws lakhs of devotees during the Bhadrapad fair.',
    'ramgarh-shekhawati' => 'Ramgarh Shekhawati in Rajasthan\'s Sikar district was built by the Poddar merchants. It is known for its painted havelis and chhatris.',
    'ramnagar' => 'Ramnagar in Nainital district is the main gateway to Jim Corbett National Park. The Garjia Devi Temple on the Kosi river and Corbett Falls are nearby.',
    'rampur-bushahr-himachal-pradesh' => 'Rampur Bushahr in Himachal Pradesh was the capital of the Bushahr state, on the Sutlej. The Padam Palace, the Lavi trade fair and the nearby Sarahan Bhimakali temple are highlights.',
    'rampur-uttar-pradesh' => 'Rampur in Uttar Pradesh was a Nawabi princely state, known for the Raza Library with its rare manuscripts and the Rampur Jama Masjid.',
    'ranakpur' => 'Ranakpur in Rajasthan\'s Pali district is home to the Ranakpur Jain Temple, famous for its 1,444 uniquely carved marble pillars. The Sun Temple and Kumbhalgarh are nearby.',
    'ranikhet' => 'Ranikhet in Uttarakhand is a peaceful cantonment hill station and home of the Kumaon Regiment. The Jhula Devi temple, Chaubatia orchards and one of Asia\'s highest golf courses are the highlights.',
    'ranthambore' => 'Ranthambore National Park in Rajasthan is one of India\'s best places to see wild tigers. The ancient Ranthambore Fort and the Trinetra Ganesh Temple inside the park are also worth a visit.',
    'ratangarh' => 'Ratangarh is a town in Churu district of Rajasthan, known for its havelis. It is easily combined with trips to Churu and Salasar.',
    'ratlam' => 'Ratlam in Madhya Pradesh is known for its namkeen (Ratlami sev) and gold market. The Kedareshwar temple and the Cactus Garden at Sailana are nearby.',
    'reengus' => 'Reengus is a town in Sikar district of Rajasthan and the nearest railway station to Khatu Shyam Ji, about 17 km away.',
    'reetha-sahib' => 'Reetha Sahib in Champawat district of Uttarakhand is a gurdwara where Guru Nanak Dev Ji is said to have turned bitter reetha fruit sweet. It is set by the Lohawati river in the Kumaon hills.',
    'renuka-ji-himachal-pradesh' => 'Renuka Ji in Sirmaur district is the largest natural lake in Himachal Pradesh, shaped like a sleeping woman. The Parshuram Tal and the Renuka wildlife sanctuary are beside it.',
    'rewalsar' => 'Rewalsar near Mandi in Himachal Pradesh is a lake holy to Buddhists, Hindus and Sikhs. A giant Padmasambhava statue, monasteries and a gurdwara overlook the lake.',
    'rewari' => 'Rewari is a district town in southern Haryana, known for its brass work. The Rewari Railway Heritage Museum and Rao Tula Ram\'s memorial are local sights.',
    'ringas' => 'Ringas is a railway town in Sikar district of Rajasthan, about 17 km from Khatu Shyam Ji.',
    'rohad' => 'Rohad is a small town in Jhajjar district of Haryana near Bahadurgarh. It is easily combined with trips to Bahadurgarh and Rohtak.',
    'rohru' => 'Rohru in Shimla district of Himachal Pradesh lies on the Pabbar river, known for trout fishing and apple orchards. The Hatkoti Durga temple is nearby.',
    'rohtak' => 'Rohtak is a major city in Haryana, known for its universities and sports. Tilyar Lake and the Asthal Bohar Math are local sights.',
    'rohtang-la-pass' => 'Rohtang Pass, at about 3,980 m above Manali in Himachal Pradesh, is famous for snow fields with views of glaciers and peaks. A permit is needed to drive up; it is usually open from May/June to October.',
    'roorkee' => 'Roorkee in Uttarakhand is home to IIT Roorkee and the historic Ganga Canal. The Piran Kaliyar Sharif dargah is nearby.',
    'ropar' => 'Ropar (Rupnagar) in Punjab sits on the Sutlej at the foot of the Shivaliks. The Ropar wetland and the Harappan-site museum are its main attractions.',
    'rudraprayag' => 'Rudraprayag in Uttarakhand is where the Alaknanda meets the Mandakini. It is a key stop on the way to Kedarnath, and the Koteshwar cave temple is nearby.',
    'rudrapur' => 'Rudrapur is the headquarters of Udham Singh Nagar district in Uttarakhand and a big industrial hub. The Atariya Devi temple is a local landmark.',
    'rupaidiha' => 'Rupaidiha in Bahraich district of Uttar Pradesh is a border town facing Nepalgunj in Nepal. It is a common crossing point for travellers to western Nepal.',
    'ruthiyai' => 'Ruthiyai is a railway junction town in Guna district of Madhya Pradesh. It is easily combined with trips to Guna.',
    'sabathu' => 'Subathu is a small cantonment hill town in Solan district of Himachal Pradesh, home to an old Gorkha Fort.',
    'sadri' => 'Sadri is a town in Pali district of Rajasthan, about 10 km from the Ranakpur Jain Temple. The Jawai leopard area is nearby.',
    'sadulpur' => 'Sadulpur (Rajgarh) is a town in Churu district of Rajasthan near the Haryana border. It is easily combined with trips to Churu and Hisar.',
    'sagar-madhya-pradesh' => 'Sagar in Madhya Pradesh is built around the Lakha Banjara Lake. The Rahatgarh waterfall and the ancient Eran site are nearby.',
    'saharanpur' => 'Saharanpur in Uttar Pradesh is famous for its wood carving. The Shakumbhari Devi temple and Company Garden are its main sights.',
    'sahaswan' => 'Sahaswan is a town in Badaun district of Uttar Pradesh. It is easily combined with trips to Badaun.',
    'salasar' => 'Salasar Balaji in Rajasthan\'s Churu district is one of the most famous Hanuman temples in north India, where the idol has a beard and moustache. Devotees often combine it with Khatu Shyam.',
    'samalkha' => 'Samalkha is a town in Panipat district of Haryana on the GT Road. It is easily combined with trips to Panipat.',
    'sambhal' => 'Sambhal is a historic city in western Uttar Pradesh, associated in Hindu belief with Kalki, the future avatar of Vishnu. The Kalki Dham is a local pilgrimage site.',
    'sampla' => 'Sampla is a town in Rohtak district of Haryana, birthplace of Sir Chhotu Ram, whose memorial is here.',
    'samrala' => 'Samrala is a town in Ludhiana district of Punjab. It is easily combined with trips to Ludhiana and Chandigarh.',
    'sandila' => 'Sandila is a town in Hardoi district of Uttar Pradesh, famous for its laddoos. It lies on the route between Lucknow and Hardoi.',
    'sangrur' => 'Sangrur is a district town in Punjab, once part of the Jind princely state. The Banasar Garden with its marble baradari is a local landmark.',
    'sankri' => 'Sankri in Uttarkashi district of Uttarakhand is the base village for the Kedarkantha and Har Ki Dun treks, inside the Govind National Park.',
    'sardarshahar' => 'Sardarshahar in Rajasthan\'s Churu district is known for its painted havelis and old merchant mansions.',
    'sardhana' => 'Sardhana near Meerut is known for the Basilica of Our Lady of Graces, built by Begum Samru, and her palace.',
    'sariska' => 'Sariska Tiger Reserve in Rajasthan\'s Alwar district lies in the Aravallis. Jeep safaris, the Kankwari Fort and the Neelkanth temples make it an easy wildlife trip from Delhi.',
    'sarsawa' => 'Sarsawa is a town in Saharanpur district of Uttar Pradesh. It is easily combined with trips to Saharanpur and Yamuna Nagar.',
    'sarwar' => 'Sarwar is a town in Ajmer district of Rajasthan, known for its Sufi dargah.',
    'satna' => 'Satna in Madhya Pradesh is known for its cement industry. The Maihar Sharda Devi temple and Chitrakoot are nearby.',
    'satpuli' => 'Satpuli is a small town in Pauri Garhwal, Uttarakhand, on the Nayar river. It lies on the route from Kotdwar into the Garhwal hills.',
    'sattal' => 'Sattal near Bhimtal in Uttarakhand is a cluster of seven connected lakes in oak and pine forest. It is a favourite with birdwatchers and nature lovers.',
    'sawai-madhopur' => 'Sawai Madhopur in Rajasthan is the gateway to Ranthambore National Park. The Ranthambore Fort and the Trinetra Ganesh Temple are the main sights.',
    'sehore' => 'Sehore near Bhopal in Madhya Pradesh is known for the Kubereshwar Dham. Bhopal is about 40 km away.',
    'seohara' => 'Seohara is a town in Bijnor district of Uttar Pradesh. It is easily combined with trips to Bijnor and Moradabad.',
    'sewagram' => 'Sevagram near Wardha in Maharashtra is where Mahatma Gandhi lived and worked from 1936. The Sevagram Ashram and Vinoba Bhave\'s Paunar Ashram are the main sights. It is a long-distance trip from Delhi.',
    'shahabad-markanda' => 'Shahabad Markanda is a town in Kurukshetra district of Haryana. The Markandeshwar temple is a local landmark.',
    'shahjahanpur' => 'Shahjahanpur in Uttar Pradesh is the birthplace of freedom fighters Ram Prasad Bismil and Ashfaqulla Khan. The Shaheed Smarak and Hanuman Dham are local sights.',
    'shahpura' => 'Shahpura is a town on the Delhi–Jaipur highway near Jaipur. It is close to Bhangarh and Shahpura Bagh.',
    'shamli' => 'Shamli is a district town in western Uttar Pradesh, known for its sugar mills. It is easily combined with trips to Muzaffarnagar and Kairana.',
    'shekhawati' => 'Shekhawati in north-east Rajasthan is famous for its painted havelis, often called the world\'s largest open-air art gallery. Mandawa, Nawalgarh, Fatehpur and Jhunjhunu are the main towns.',
    'shikohabad' => 'Shikohabad is a town in Firozabad district of Uttar Pradesh. It is easily combined with trips to Firozabad and Agra.',
    'shikrapur' => 'Shikrapur is a town near Pune in Maharashtra, on the Pune–Ahmednagar road. The Ranjangaon Ganpati temple is nearby. It is a long-distance trip from Delhi.',
    'shivpuri' => 'Shivpuri in Madhya Pradesh was the summer capital of the Scindias. Madhav National Park, the marble Scindia Chhatris and Sakhya Sagar lake are the highlights.',
    'siddhpur' => 'Sidhpur in north Gujarat is known for the Rudra Mahalaya ruins, Bindu Sarovar (for matru shraddh) and colourful Bohra havelis.',
    'sidhauli' => 'Sidhauli is a town in Sitapur district of Uttar Pradesh. It is easily combined with trips to Sitapur and Lucknow.',
    'sikandrabad' => 'Sikandrabad is a town in Bulandshahr district of Uttar Pradesh, near Greater Noida. It is easily combined with trips to Bulandshahr.',
    'sikar' => 'Sikar is a city in Rajasthan\'s Shekhawati region, known for its havelis and coaching institutes. The Harshnath and Jeen Mata temples and Khatu Shyam Ji are nearby.',
    'sirhind-fatehgarh-sahib' => 'Sirhind (Fatehgarh Sahib) in Punjab is where the younger Sahibzadas of Guru Gobind Singh Ji were martyred. Gurdwara Fatehgarh Sahib, the Rauza Sharif and the Aam Khas Bagh are the main sights.',
    'siriyari' => 'Siriyari is a village in Pali district of Rajasthan, an important Jain pilgrimage site with the samadhi of Acharya Bhikshu.',
    'sirmaur' => 'Sirmaur district in Himachal Pradesh, with Nahan as its headquarters, is known for Renuka Ji lake, the Churdhar peak and Paonta Sahib.',
    'sirohi-road' => 'Sirohi Road (Pindwara) is a railway town in Rajasthan\'s Sirohi district, a gateway to Mount Abu and the Ajari temple.',
    'sirsa' => 'Sirsa is a district town in Haryana near the Punjab border. It is known for the Dera Sacha Sauda and the Tara Baba Kutiya.',
    'sirsaganj' => 'Sirsaganj is a town in Firozabad district of Uttar Pradesh. It is easily combined with trips to Firozabad and Etawah.',
    'sitapur' => 'Sitapur is a district town in Uttar Pradesh between Lucknow and Shahjahanpur. The holy site of Naimisharanya is about 35 km away.',
    'sitarganj' => 'Sitarganj is a town in Udham Singh Nagar district of Uttarakhand. The Nanakmatta Sahib gurdwara is nearby.',
    'sohna' => 'Sohna near Gurugram in Haryana is known for its sulphur hot springs and the Aravalli hills. Damdama Lake is close by.',
    'sojat' => 'Sojat in Rajasthan\'s Pali district is famous for its henna (mehndi), grown on large farms around the town. The Sojat Fort and Chamunda Mata temple overlook it.',
    'sojat-road' => 'Sojat Road is a railway station town in Pali district of Rajasthan, about 10 km from Sojat. It is easily combined with trips to Pali and Jodhpur.',
    'solan' => 'Solan in Himachal Pradesh is called the "Mushroom City of India". The Shoolini Mata temple and Karol Tibba are its main sights, and Chail and Kasauli are nearby.',
    'solang' => 'Solang Valley near Manali in Himachal Pradesh is an adventure hub with paragliding, the Solang ropeway and skiing in winter. It is close to the south portal of the Atal Tunnel.',
    'someshwar' => 'Someshwar is a small town in Almora district of Uttarakhand, about 15 km from Kausani. The ancient Someshwar temple gives the town its name.',
    'sonipat' => 'Sonipat is a city in Haryana just north of Delhi, known for its universities. The famous dhabas of Murthal are part of the district.',
    'spiti-valley' => 'Spiti Valley in Himachal Pradesh is a high-altitude cold desert between Tibet and India. Key Monastery, Dhankar, Tabo, Kibber, Langza and Chandratal lake make it a dream road trip, best done from June to October.',
    'sri-dungargarh' => 'Sri Dungargarh is a town in Bikaner district of Rajasthan, on the Bikaner–Ratangarh road. It is easily combined with trips to Bikaner.',
    'sri-ganganagar' => 'Sri Ganganagar is the northernmost city of Rajasthan, known as the "Food Basket of Rajasthan" thanks to the Gang Canal. The Hindumalkot border and the Laila Majnu Mazar are nearby.',
    'srinagar-uttarakhand' => 'Srinagar (Garhwal) is a town in Uttarakhand on the Alaknanda river, home to HNB Garhwal University. The Dhari Devi temple and the Kamleshwar Mahadev temple are its main sights.',
    'sujangarh' => 'Sujangarh in Rajasthan\'s Churu district lies close to Salasar Balaji and the Tal Chhapar blackbuck sanctuary.',
    'sultana' => 'Sultana is a small place in Rajasthan. Share your exact location and we will plan the best route and pickup timing for your group.',
    'sultanpur' => 'Sultanpur is a district town in eastern Uttar Pradesh on the Gomti river. The Vijethua Mahavira Dham and Sita Kund are local religious sites.',
    'sultanpur-lodhi' => 'Sultanpur Lodhi in Kapurthala district of Punjab is where Guru Nanak Dev Ji is said to have received enlightenment. The Gurdwara Ber Sahib and the Kanjli wetland are nearby.',
    'sumerpur' => 'Sumerpur in Pali district of Rajasthan is the gateway to the Jawai leopard area and the Jawai Dam.',
    'sunam' => 'Sunam in Punjab\'s Sangrur district is the hometown of Shaheed Udham Singh, whose memorial stands here.',
    'sunauli' => 'Sonauli in Maharajganj district of Uttar Pradesh is the main India–Nepal border crossing. Lumbini, the birthplace of the Buddha, is about 25 km across the border.',
    'sundar-nagar' => 'Sundernagar in Mandi district of Himachal Pradesh is known for its large lake and the Suketi Fossil Park. The Mahamaya temple overlooks the town.',
    'surajpur' => 'Surajpur in Greater Noida, Uttar Pradesh, is known for the Surajpur Bird Sanctuary and wetland.',
    'talwara' => 'Talwara in Punjab\'s Hoshiarpur district is next to the Pong Dam on the Beas. The Kamahi Devi temple is nearby.',
    'tanakpur' => 'Tanakpur in Uttarakhand\'s Champawat district sits on the Sharda river at the Nepal border. It is the base for the Purnagiri temple.',
    'tanda-urmar' => 'Tanda Urmar is a town in Hoshiarpur district of Punjab. It is easily combined with trips to Hoshiarpur and Jalandhar.',
    'tarn-taran' => 'Tarn Taran near Amritsar is home to the Sri Darbar Sahib Tarn Taran, which has the largest sarovar (holy tank) of any gurdwara. The Harike wetland is nearby.',
    'tehri-garhwal' => 'Tehri in Uttarakhand is known for the Tehri Dam, one of the tallest in India, and Tehri Lake with boating, jet-skiing and other water sports. The Koteshwar temple is nearby.',
    'thanesar' => 'Thanesar, the old town of Kurukshetra in Haryana, was the capital of King Harshavardhana. The Sthaneshwar Mahadev temple, Brahma Sarovar and Sheikh Chilli\'s Tomb are the main sights.',
    'theog' => 'Theog is a hill town on the Shimla–Narkanda road in Himachal Pradesh, surrounded by apple orchards.',
    'tijara' => 'Tijara in Rajasthan\'s Alwar district is known for its Jain temple and the Tijara Fort Palace heritage hotel. It is an easy getaway from Delhi and Gurugram.',
    'timilimansingh' => 'Timili Mansingh is a small place in Uttarakhand. Share your exact location and we will plan the best route and pickup timing for your group.',
    'tirthan-valley' => 'Tirthan Valley in Kullu district of Himachal Pradesh is a peaceful valley along the Tirthan river at the edge of the Great Himalayan National Park. Jibhi, Jalori Pass and trout fishing make it a great offbeat escape.',
    'tiuni' => 'Tiuni is a small town in Dehradun district of Uttarakhand on the Tons river. The Hanol Mahasu Devta temple is about 10 km away.',
    'tohana' => 'Tohana is a town in Fatehabad district of Haryana. It is easily combined with trips to Jind and Fatehabad.',
    'tonk' => 'Tonk in Rajasthan was a Nawabi state, known for the Sunehri Kothi and its Arabic and Persian Research Institute. The Bisalpur Dam is nearby.',
    'toopran' => 'Toopran is a town in Medak district of Telangana, north of Hyderabad. The Medak Cathedral is nearby. It is a long-distance trip from Delhi, best planned over several days.',
    'tulsipur' => 'Tulsipur in Balrampur district of Uttar Pradesh is home to the Devipatan Shaktipeeth temple.',
    'tundla' => 'Tundla is a railway junction town near Agra in Firozabad district. It is a common pickup point for travellers arriving by train.',
    'udaipur-airport' => 'Udaipur\'s Maharana Pratap Airport (Dabok) is about 25 km from the city. We pick up and drop groups at the airport for Udaipur, Nathdwara and Kumbhalgarh tours.',
    'udhampur' => 'Udhampur is a town in Jammu and Kashmir on the Jammu–Srinagar route and a major army base. Patnitop and the Krimchi temples are nearby.',
    'ujhani' => 'Ujhani is a town in Badaun district of Uttar Pradesh. It is easily combined with trips to Badaun.',
    'ujjain' => 'Ujjain in Madhya Pradesh is home to the Mahakaleshwar Jyotirlinga, famous for its Bhasma Aarti, and hosts the Simhastha Kumbh. Ram Ghat on the Shipra, the Kal Bhairav temple and the Mahakal Lok corridor are highlights.',
    'ukhimath' => 'Ukhimath in Rudraprayag district is the winter seat of Lord Kedarnath at the Omkareshwar Temple. Chopta and Deoria Tal are nearby.',
    'una' => 'Una in Himachal Pradesh lies on the Swan river near the Punjab border. It is the gateway to the Chintpurni temple and the Dera Baba Barbhag Singh.',
    'unchahar' => 'Unchahar is a town in Raebareli district of Uttar Pradesh, known for the NTPC power plant.',
    'unnao' => 'Unnao is a district town in Uttar Pradesh between Kanpur and Lucknow. The Nawabganj bird sanctuary is nearby.',
    'uttarkashi' => 'Uttarkashi in Uttarakhand sits on the Bhagirathi river on the way to Gangotri. The Kashi Vishwanath temple, the Nehru Institute of Mountaineering and the Dodital trek are its highlights.',
    'vaishno-devi' => 'Vaishno Devi is one of India\'s most visited shrines, a cave temple of Mata Vaishno Devi in the Trikuta hills above Katra, Jammu and Kashmir. Pilgrims trek about 12 km from Katra to the Bhawan, with Ardhkuwari and the Bhairon temple on the way.',
    'vasind' => 'Vasind is a town in Thane district of Maharashtra on the Mumbai–Nashik route, beside the Bhatsa river. It is a long-distance trip from Delhi.',
    'vidisha' => 'Vidisha in Madhya Pradesh is an ancient city near Sanchi. The Udayagiri caves and the Heliodorus Pillar are its main historic sites.',
    'vikasnagar' => 'Vikasnagar is a town in Dehradun district of Uttarakhand, close to Dakpatthar and the Kalsi Ashokan edict.',
    'visveshwara-nagar' => 'Visveshwara Nagar is a small place in Uttar Pradesh. Share your exact location and we will plan the best route and pickup timing for your group.',
    'vrindavan' => 'Vrindavan, where Lord Krishna spent his childhood, is home to thousands of temples. Banke Bihari, Prem Mandir, ISKCON Vrindavan and Nidhivan are the highlights, and it is one of the most popular day trips from Delhi.',
    'wagah-border' => 'The Attari–Wagah border near Amritsar is famous for the Beating Retreat ceremony held every evening by the BSF and Pakistan Rangers. The Golden Temple is about 30 km away.',
    'yamuna-nagar' => 'Yamuna Nagar is an industrial city in Haryana on the Yamuna, known for its plywood industry. Kalesar National Park, Hathnikund barrage and Adi Badri are nearby.',
    'yamunotri' => 'Yamunotri is the first of the Char Dham shrines, at the source of the Yamuna in Uttarkashi district. The road ends at Janki Chatti, from where pilgrims trek about 6 km to the temple and the Surya Kund hot spring.',
    'zirakpur' => 'Zirakpur in Punjab\'s Mohali district sits at the gateway to Chandigarh, Shimla and Patiala. Chandigarh is just 10 km away.',
